## 🎯 Next.js App Router Best Practices

### Server vs Client Components

**Default to Server Components:**
- ✅ Use Server Components by default (no 'use client' directive)
- ✅ Server Components can directly access backend resources (Supabase server client)
- ✅ Server Components reduce JavaScript bundle size
- ✅ Server Components improve SEO and initial page load

**Use Client Components Only When Needed:**
- ✅ Interactive features (onClick, onChange, useState, useEffect)
- ✅ Browser APIs (localStorage, window, document)
- ✅ React hooks (useState, useEffect, useRef, useContext)
- ✅ Event listeners
- ✅ Third-party libraries that require client-side rendering

**Pattern:**
```typescript
// ✅ Good: Server Component (default)
export default function Section() {
  const data = await fetchData() // Can use async/await
  return <div>{data}</div>
}

// ✅ Good: Client Component (when needed)
'use client'
export default function InteractiveButton() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0)
  return <button onClick={() => setCount(count + 1)}>{count}</button>
}

// ✅ Good: Composition - Server Component wrapping Client Component
export default function Page() {
  return (
    <div>
      <ServerContent />
      <ClientInteractiveComponent />
    </div>
  )
}
```

### Data Fetching

**Server Components:**
- ✅ Use async/await directly in Server Components
- ✅ Fetch data at the component level, not in useEffect
- ✅ Use Supabase server client (`lib/supabase/server.ts`) in Server Components
- ✅ Revalidate data when needed using `revalidate` or `revalidatePath`

**Client Components:**
- ✅ Use React Query or SWR for client-side data fetching
- ✅ Or use Server Actions for mutations
- ❌ Don't fetch data in useEffect for initial render (use Server Components)

**Pattern:**
```typescript
// ✅ Good: Server Component data fetching
export default async function RSVPList() {
  const { data } = await supabaseServer.from('rsvps').select()
  return <div>{/* render data */}</div>
}

// ✅ Good: Server Action for mutations
'use server'
export async function submitRSVP(formData: FormData) {
  // Server-side logic
}
```

### Route Handlers (API Routes)

**Best Practices:**
- ✅ Use Route Handlers (`app/api/route.ts`) for external API integrations
- ✅ Use Server Actions for form submissions and mutations (preferred)
- ✅ Always validate input with Zod before processing
- ✅ Return proper HTTP status codes (200, 400, 401, 500)
- ✅ Use consistent error response format
- ✅ Implement rate limiting for public endpoints
- ✅ Use Supabase service role key only in API routes, never expose to client

**Pattern:**
```typescript
// ✅ Good: Route Handler
export async function POST(request: Request) {
  try {
    const body = await request.json()
    const validated = schema.parse(body)
    // Process...
    return NextResponse.json({ success: true }, { status: 200 })
  } catch (error) {
    return NextResponse.json(
      { error: 'Invalid request' },
      { status: 400 }
    )
  }
}

// ✅ Better: Server Action (for forms)
'use server'
export async function submitForm(formData: FormData) {
  const data = Object.fromEntries(formData)
  const validated = schema.parse(data)
  // Process...
}
```

### Images & Assets

**Image Optimization:**
- ✅ Always use `next/image` component, never `<img>` tag
- ✅ Provide `width` and `height` or use `fill` with parent container
- ✅ Use `priority` prop for above-the-fold images
- ✅ Use `sizes` prop for responsive images
- ✅ Use appropriate `quality` (default 75, can go lower for decorative images)
- ✅ Prefer WebP format when possible

**Pattern:**
```typescript
// ✅ Good: Next.js Image
import Image from 'next/image'

<Image
  src="/images/couple.jpg"
  alt="Couple photo"
  width={1920}
  height={1080}
  priority // For hero images
  sizes="100vw"
  className="object-cover"
/>

// ✅ Good: Fill image
<div className="relative w-full h-64">
  <Image
    src="/images/bg.jpg"
    alt="Background"
    fill
    className="object-cover"
    sizes="100vw"
  />
</div>
```

### Metadata & SEO

**Static Metadata:**
- ✅ Export `metadata` object from layout.tsx and page.tsx
- ✅ Include title, description, openGraph, twitter cards
- ✅ Use dynamic metadata when needed with `generateMetadata` function

**Pattern:**
```typescript
// ✅ Good: Static metadata
export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: 'Wedding 2026',
  description: 'Join us for our special day',
  openGraph: {
    title: 'Wedding 2026',
    description: 'Join us for our special day',
    images: ['/images/og-image.jpg'],
  },
}

// ✅ Good: Dynamic metadata
export async function generateMetadata(): Promise<Metadata> {
  return {
    title: `${couple.name1} & ${couple.name2} Wedding`,
  }
}
```

### Loading & Error States

**Loading States:**
- ✅ Create `loading.tsx` files for automatic loading UI
- ✅ Use Suspense boundaries for granular loading states
- ✅ Show skeleton loaders, not just spinners
- ✅ Use `loading.tsx` in route segments

**Error Handling:**
- ✅ Create `error.tsx` files for error boundaries
- ✅ Use `error.tsx` with error and reset props
- ✅ Log errors appropriately (server-side)
- ✅ Show user-friendly error messages

**Pattern:**
```typescript
// ✅ Good: loading.tsx
export default function Loading() {
  return <div>Loading...</div>
}

// ✅ Good: error.tsx
'use client'
export default function Error({
  error,
  reset,
}: {
  error: Error & { digest?: string }
  reset: () => void
}) {
  return (
    <div>
      <h2>Something went wrong!</h2>
      <button onClick={() => reset()}>Try again</button>
    </div>
  )
}
```

### Caching & Revalidation

**Caching Strategy:**
- ✅ Use `cache()` for request deduplication
- ✅ Use `unstable_cache` for custom caching
- ✅ Understand `fetch` caching options (default, no-store, force-cache)
- ✅ Use `revalidate` for time-based revalidation
- ✅ Use `revalidatePath` or `revalidateTag` for on-demand revalidation

**Pattern:**
```typescript
// ✅ Good: Cached data fetching
import { cache } from 'react'

export const getWeddingData = cache(async () => {
  const data = await fetch('...', { next: { revalidate: 3600 } })
  return data.json()
})
```

