## 📁 File Structure & Organization

### Directory Structure
```
app/
  ├── (routes)/          # Route groups (optional)
  ├── api/               # API routes
  │   └── [route]/route.ts
  ├── layout.tsx         # Root layout
  ├── page.tsx           # Home page
  ├── loading.tsx        # Loading UI
  ├── error.tsx          # Error boundary
  └── not-found.tsx     # 404 page

components/
  ├── sections/          # Page sections
  ├── forms/             # Form components
  ├── decorations/       # Decoration components
  └── [shared]/          # Shared components

lib/
  ├── supabase/          # Supabase clients
  ├── validations/       # Zod schemas
  ├── colors/            # Color utilities
  └── utils/             # General utilities

types/                   # TypeScript types
config/                  # Configuration files
hooks/                   # Custom React hooks
```

### Naming Conventions
- ✅ Use PascalCase for components: `RSVPForm.tsx`
- ✅ Use camelCase for utilities: `formatDate.ts`
- ✅ Use kebab-case for routes: `app/rsvp/page.tsx`
- ✅ Use descriptive names: `PersonFormSection.tsx` not `Form1.tsx`
- ✅ Prefix hooks with `use`: `useColors.ts`
- ✅ Prefix types/interfaces appropriately: `RSVPFormData`, `SectionProps`

---

## 🎨 Component Best Practices

### Component Structure
```typescript
// ✅ Good: Well-structured component
'use client' // Only if needed

import { useState } from 'react'
import type { ComponentProps } from './types'

interface Props {
  title: string
  onSubmit: (data: FormData) => void
}

export default function Component({ title, onSubmit }: Props) {
  // 1. Hooks
  const [state, setState] = useState()
  
  // 2. Event handlers
  const handleSubmit = () => { /* ... */ }
  
  // 3. Render
  return (
    <div>
      {/* JSX */}
    </div>
  )
}
```

### Component Guidelines
- ✅ One component per file
- ✅ Export components as default
- ✅ Use TypeScript interfaces for props (not types for props)
- ✅ Keep components under 200 lines (extract sub-components)
- ✅ Extract complex logic into custom hooks
- ✅ Use composition over prop drilling
- ✅ Include JSDoc comments for complex components
- ✅ Co-locate related components (e.g., `FormField.tsx` and `FormField.test.tsx`)

### Props & Types
```typescript
// ✅ Good: Interface for props
interface ButtonProps {
  children: React.ReactNode
  onClick: () => void
  variant?: 'primary' | 'secondary'
  disabled?: boolean
}

// ✅ Good: Extend HTML attributes when needed
interface InputProps extends React.InputHTMLAttributes<HTMLInputElement> {
  label: string
  error?: string
}

// ✅ Good: Use type for unions, interfaces for objects
type Size = 'small' | 'medium' | 'large'
interface ComponentProps {
  size: Size
}
```

