## 🔒 Security Best Practices

### Environment Variables
- ✅ Never commit `.env.local` or `.env`
- ✅ Use `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix only for client-safe variables
- ✅ Use server-only variables without prefix (never exposed to client)
- ✅ Validate environment variables at startup
- ✅ Use different keys for development and production

### Input Validation
- ✅ Always validate on server-side (Zod schemas)
- ✅ Sanitize user input before database operations
- ✅ Use parameterized queries (Supabase handles this)
- ✅ Never trust client-side validation alone

### API Security
- ✅ Use Supabase RLS (Row Level Security) policies
- ✅ Validate authentication in API routes
- ✅ Implement rate limiting for public endpoints
- ✅ Use CSRF tokens for state-changing operations
- ✅ Never expose service role keys to client

---

## ⚡ Performance Optimization

### Code Splitting
- ✅ Use dynamic imports for heavy components: `const Heavy = dynamic(() => import('./Heavy'))`
- ✅ Lazy load components below the fold
- ✅ Split large libraries (import only what you need)

### Bundle Optimization
- ✅ Use `next/dynamic` with `ssr: false` for client-only components
- ✅ Avoid importing entire libraries (use tree-shaking)
- ✅ Use React.memo for expensive components
- ✅ Use useMemo/useCallback appropriately (don't overuse)

### Rendering Optimization
- ✅ Use Server Components to reduce client bundle
- ✅ Implement proper loading states (avoid layout shift)
- ✅ Optimize images (next/image handles this)
- ✅ Use `font-display: swap` for web fonts
- ✅ Minimize re-renders with proper state management

---

## 🧪 TypeScript Best Practices

### Type Safety
- ✅ Use `strict: true` in tsconfig.json
- ✅ Avoid `any` type (use `unknown` if needed)
- ✅ Use type guards for runtime validation
- ✅ Prefer interfaces for object shapes
- ✅ Use type aliases for unions/primitives
- ✅ Export types from `types/` directory

### Type Patterns
```typescript
// ✅ Good: Proper typing
interface User {
  id: string
  name: string
  email: string
}

// ✅ Good: Type guards
function isUser(obj: unknown): obj is User {
  return typeof obj === 'object' && obj !== null && 'id' in obj
}

// ✅ Good: Utility types
type PartialUser = Partial<User>
type UserEmail = Pick<User, 'email'>
```

---

## 🎯 Code Style & Conventions

### General Rules
- ✅ Use functional components with hooks
- ✅ Use meaningful variable and function names
- ✅ Keep functions small and focused (single responsibility)
- ✅ Extract magic numbers/strings to constants
- ✅ Use early returns to reduce nesting
- ✅ Prefer const over let, avoid var

### Tailwind CSS
- ✅ Use utility classes, avoid inline styles
- ✅ Create reusable component classes when needed
- ✅ Use responsive prefixes (sm:, md:, lg:)
- ✅ Mobile-first approach
- ✅ Use arbitrary values sparingly: `bg-[#custom]`
- ✅ Extract repeated patterns to component classes

### Comments & Documentation
- ✅ Write self-documenting code (clear names > comments)
- ✅ Add JSDoc for complex functions/components
- ✅ Comment "why" not "what"
- ✅ Keep comments up-to-date with code changes
- ✅ Remove commented-out code before committing

---

## 🧩 React Patterns

### Hooks Best Practices
- ✅ Follow Rules of Hooks (top-level only, same order)
- ✅ Extract custom hooks for reusable logic
- ✅ Use useMemo for expensive calculations
- ✅ Use useCallback for stable function references (when passing to memoized children)
- ✅ Clean up effects (return cleanup function)
- ✅ Don't overuse useMemo/useCallback (profile first)

### State Management
- ✅ Use useState for local component state
- ✅ Use useReducer for complex state logic
- ✅ Use Context for shared state (avoid prop drilling)
- ✅ Consider Zustand/Jotai for global state if needed
- ✅ Keep state as close to usage as possible

### Event Handlers
- ✅ Use descriptive handler names: `handleSubmit`, `onClick`
- ✅ Extract complex handlers to separate functions
- ✅ Use arrow functions or useCallback appropriately
- ✅ Pass event handlers as props with `on` prefix: `onClick`, `onChange`

---

## 📝 Forms & Validation

### React Hook Form
- ✅ Use React Hook Form for all forms
- ✅ Validate with Zod schemas (@hookform/resolvers)
- ✅ Show field-level errors
- ✅ Disable submit button during submission
- ✅ Show loading states
- ✅ Handle success/error states gracefully

### Form Patterns
```typescript
// ✅ Good: Form with validation
const schema = z.object({
  email: z.string().email(),
  name: z.string().min(1),
})

const { register, handleSubmit, formState: { errors } } = useForm({
  resolver: zodResolver(schema),
})

// ✅ Good: Server Action integration
const onSubmit = async (data: FormData) => {
  'use server'
  const validated = schema.parse(data)
  // Process...
}
```

---

## 🗄️ Database & Supabase

### Supabase Patterns
- ✅ Use server client (`lib/supabase/server.ts`) in Server Components
- ✅ Use client (`lib/supabase/client.ts`) only in Client Components
- ✅ Always use RLS policies
- ✅ Use transactions for multi-step operations
- ✅ Handle errors properly (check error.code)
- ✅ Use TypeScript types from Supabase CLI when possible

### Query Patterns
```typescript
// ✅ Good: Server Component query
const { data, error } = await supabaseServer
  .from('rsvps')
  .select('*')
  .eq('attending', true)

if (error) {
  // Handle error
}

// ✅ Good: Error handling
try {
  const { data, error } = await supabaseServer.from('table').select()
  if (error) throw error
  return data
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Database error:', error)
  throw new Error('Failed to fetch data')
}
```

